  "solution": "**Given:**\n\nInstallments X = ₹750\n\nNumber of years N = 5\n\nRate of simple interest R = 5%\n\n**Formula used:**\n\nX = P × 100 / [(N × 100) + {(N-1) + (N-2) + (N-3) + …. + 1} × R)]\n\n**Calculation:**\n\nSum of series = (5-1) + (5-2) + (5-3) + (5-4) + 1 = 4 + 3 + 2 + 1 = 10\n\nX = P × 100 / [(N × 100) + {(N-1) + (N-2) + (N-3) + …. + 1} × R)]\n\n750 = P × 100 / [(5 × 100) + {10} × 5]\n\n⇒ 750 = P × 100 / [500 + 50]\n\n⇒ 750 = P × 100 / 550\n\n⇒ 750 = P × 10 / 55\n\n⇒ P = 4125\n\n**The debt is ₹4125.**\n\n49:T",
